arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App shipment tracker in /tmp/sv-be1ac3272e60443b8a9be108b744b6a2/ShipmentTracker/. The project was scaffolded with `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`. It has two projects:

- **ShipmentTracker** (server): hosts the app, EF Core, API endpoints
- **ShipmentTracker.Client** (WebAssembly): all interactive UI components

Key architecture rules for Auto Global mode:
- Interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project
- Components cannot access DbContext directly — use HTTP APIs
- Both Program.cs files must register matching services
- No `@rendermode` needed on pages (global mode)

The existing project has:
- Identity auth configured with SQLite
- ApplicationDbContext in ShipmentTracker/Data/
- Template pages (Counter, Weather, Auth) in ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/ that need to be replaced

## What to implement:

### 1. Remove template pages
Delete Counter.razor, Weather.razor, Auth.razor from ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/

### 2. Shared Models (create in ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/)

**ShipmentStatus.cs:**
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Exception
}
```

**Shipment.cs:**
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string RecipientName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### 3. Service Interface (ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs)

```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<Shipment?> GetByIdAsync(int id);
    Task UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 4. Client-side implementation (ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs)

Uses HttpClient to call server API endpoints:
- GET /api/shipments
- GET /api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}
- GET /api/shipments/{id}
- PUT /api/shipments/{id}/status

### 5. Server-side implementation (ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentServerService.cs)

Uses ApplicationDbContext directly to query shipments.

### 6. Update ApplicationDbContext (ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs)

Add `DbSet<Shipment>` — reference the model from .Client project. Add the entity configuration (the server project already references the client project).

Actually, since the server project references the .Client project assembly (for `AddAdditionalAssemblies`), it can use the Shipment model from there.

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ApplicationDbContext(DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options) : IdentityDbContext<ApplicationUser>(options)
{
    public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();
}
```

### 7. API Endpoints (add to server Program.cs before app.Run())

Add a shipments API group:
```csharp
var shipments = app.MapGroup("/api/shipments").RequireAuthorization();
shipments.MapGet("/", async (ApplicationDbContext db) => 
    await db.Shipments.ToListAsync());
shipments.MapGet("/track/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
    await db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber));
shipments.MapGet("/{id:int}", async (int id, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
    await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id));
shipments.MapPut("/{id:int}/status", async (int id, ShipmentStatus status, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
{
    var shipment = await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
    if (shipment is null) return Results.NotFound();
    shipment.Status = status;
    if (status == ShipmentStatus.Delivered)
        shipment.ActualDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow;
    await db.SaveChangesAsync();
    return Results.Ok(shipment);
});
```

The tracking endpoint should allow anonymous access so customers can track without logging in. Use `.AllowAnonymous()` on the track endpoint only.

### 8. Pages

**ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Home.razor** — Replace existing with a landing page:
```razor
@page "/"

<PageTitle>ShipmentTracker - Home</PageTitle>

<div class="container mt-4">
    <h1>Shipment Tracker</h1>
    <p class="lead">Track and manage your shipments worldwide.</p>

    <div class="row mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="card">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h5 class="card-title">Track a Shipment</h5>
                    <p class="card-text">Enter your tracking number to check delivery status.</p>
                    <a href="tracking" class="btn btn-primary">Track Now</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="card">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h5 class="card-title">Dispatcher Dashboard</h5>
                    <p class="card-text">View and manage all shipments.</p>
                    <a href="shipments" class="btn btn-secondary">Go to Dashboard</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
```

**ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Tracking.razor** — Customer tracking (allow anonymous):
```razor
@page "/tracking"
@page "/tracking/{TrackingNumber}"
@inject IShipmentService ShipmentService

<PageTitle>Track Shipment</PageTitle>

<div class="container mt-4">
    <h2>Track Your Shipment</h2>

    <div class="row mb-4">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="input-group">
                <input type="text" class="form-control" placeholder="Enter tracking number..."
                       @bind="searchTrackingNumber" @bind:event="oninput"
                       @onkeyup="HandleKeyUp" />
                <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="SearchShipment">
                    Search
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @if (isLoading)
    {
        <div class="spinner-border" role="status">
            <span class="visually-hidden">Loading...</span>
        </div>
    }
    else if (errorMessage is not null)
    {
        <div class="alert alert-warning">@errorMessage</div>
    }
    else if (shipment is not null)
    {
        <div class="card">
            <div class="card-header">
                <strong>Tracking #:</strong> @shipment.TrackingNumber
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <p><strong>Status:</strong> <span class="badge @GetStatusBadgeClass(shipment.Status)">@shipment.Status</span></p>
                        <p><strong>Origin:</strong> @shipment.Origin</p>
                        <p><strong>Destination:</strong> @shipment.Destination</p>
